actor out a $19$.\n\\item $p=19^5$, then $q=1$, making the numbers in the $n^2$ sums $r$ not relatively prime to $n=2$. $p+q=19^5+1$ doesn't commute $>19$ as asked.\n\\item This only takes us to $0$ sum, no divisions could make any negative.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\nFor a total of $364+210=574$ sums compatible with $p+q \\mid 2006$.",
